{"name":"I Love You Pink","hex":"#d97d8f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"},{"term":"you","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Pronoun","definitions":["The people spoken, or written to, as an object. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","(To) yourselves, (to) yourself."]},{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["The individual or group spoken or written to.","Used before epithets, describing the person being addressed, for emphasis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/you"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"I","blocks":[{"text":"I is the ninth letter and the third vowel letter of the Latin alphabet, used in the modern English alphabet, the alphabets of other western European languages and others worldwide. Its name in English is i, plural i's or is."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Latin_letter_I.svg/330px-Latin_letter_I.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I","wikidata":"Q9893"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love","wikidata":"Q316"},{"title":"You","blocks":[{"text":"In Modern English, the word \"you\" is the second-person pronoun. It is grammatically plural, and was historically used only for the dative case, but in most modern dialects is used for all cases and numbers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You","wikidata":"Q1165897"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/The_Letter_%22i%22_in_Different_European_Languages.png/500px-The_Letter_%22i%22_in_Different_European_Languages.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/The_Letter_%22i%22_in_Different_European_Languages.png/1280px-The_Letter_%22i%22_in_Different_European_Languages.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/The_Letter_%22i%22_in_Different_European_Languages.png/500px-The_Letter_%22i%22_in_Different_European_Languages.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pronunciation of the name of the letter ⟨i⟩ in European languages","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Letter_%22i%22_in_Different_European_Languages.png"},{"srcset":"https:/